            {
              "title": "Colors in Sentences",
              "weight": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "order": 1,
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "{\"time\":1700002002000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"yY5zZ6aA7b\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"In English, adjectives like colors come <b>before the noun</b> they describe.\"}},{\"id\":\"bB8cC9dD0e\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Examples:\"}},{\"id\":\"eE1fF2gG3h\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"a <b>red</b> car\",\"a <b>blue</b> shirt\",\"a <b>yellow</b> banana\",\"a <b>green</b> tree\"]}},{\"id\":\"hH4iI5jJ6k\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"We can also use colors after the verb <b>to be</b>:\"}},{\"id\":\"kK7lL8mM9n\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"The car <b>is red</b>.\",\"Her eyes <b>are blue</b>.\",\"The sky <b>is grey</b> today.\"]}},{\"id\":\"nN0oO1pP2q\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"To ask about color: <b>What color is it?</b> or <b>What color are they?</b>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
                },
                {
                  "order": 2,
                  "type": "audio",
                  "content": {
                    "text": "What color is it? It is a red car.",
                    "type": "tts",
                    "audio_url": ""
