        {
          "title": "Describing Objects by Shape",
          "weight": 4,
          "content": [
            {
              "order": 1,
              "type": "text",
              "content": "{\"time\":1700002004000,\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"cC5dD6eE7f\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"We can describe everyday objects using shape words. Look at these examples:\"}},{\"id\":\"fF8gG9hH0i\",\"type\":\"list\",\"data\":{\"style\":\"unordered\",\"items\":[\"The <b>clock</b> is round (circular).\",\"The <b>door</b> is rectangular.\",\"The <b>pizza slice</b> is triangular.\",\"The <b>window</b> is square.\"]}},{\"id\":\"iI1jJ2kK3l\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Useful question: <b>What shape is it?</b>\"}},{\"id\":\"lL4mM5nN6o\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"Useful answer: <em>It is a circle. / It is round. / It has a rectangular shape.</em>\"}}],\"version\":\"2.31.4\"}"
            },
